text:
On the shelf above the linen chest:

a shallow dish of buttons, mostly brown;
a green glass marble with a bubble inside;
a ribbon wound around two fingers, then slipped free;
the little wooden bird whose paint has worn away along its back.

The window is open. Clean sheets lift on the line outside, filling, falling, showing the garden through the spaces between them. Warm cotton brushes the sill.

A woman chooses a button, holds it against her cuff, and threads her needle. The marble stays in its dish with a small piece of the window inside it.
